# Line endings are part of the build here, not a personal preference.
#
# Sources must be LF: Vite/esbuild strips a `#!` shebang up to the *newline only*,
# so a CRLF shebang leaves a stray `\r` at the top of the file and vitest dies
# with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token". That is exactly what happened
# on the Windows runner, where git checks out with core.autocrlf=true.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell 5.1 wants CRLF (and install.ps1 carries a UTF-8 BOM), so these files
# are stored byte-for-byte and never normalised.
*.ps1 -text
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text

# Binary assets: no conversion, no diff noise.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.bmp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
